root@26d9df2e6bbd:/app# cat > /app/black/notes_for_testing.txt << 'EOF'
> Black Library - Key Functions for Testing
> 
> Black is an uncompromising Python code formatter.
> 
> Key Functions and Modules to Test:
> 1. black.format_str() - Main function to format Python code strings
> 2. black.format_file_in_place() - Format a file in place
> 3. black.reformat_many() - Format multiple files
> 4. black.lib2to3_parse() - Parse Python code using lib2to3
> 5. black.get_features_used() - Detect Python features in code
> 6. linegen.LineGenerator - Generate formatted lines from AST
> 7. strings.normalize_string() - Normalize string literals
> 8. strings.fix_docstring() - Fix docstring formatting
> 9. trans.transform_line() - Transform a line of code
> 10. comments.normalize_invisible_parens() - Handle invisible parentheses
> 11. brackets.get_implied_line_range() - Handle bracket logic
> 12. parsing.parse_ast() - Parse Python AST
> 13. Mode class - Configuration for formatting behavior
> 
> Fuzzing Focus Areas:
> - Malformed Python code handling
> - Edge cases in string normalization
> - Comment handling in various positions
> - Large/deeply nested code structures
> - Unicode and special character handling
> - Various Python syntax edge cases
> EOF
